			{
				"id": "post-canonical",
				"slug": "what-canonical-tags-can-do",
				"status": "published",
				"data": {
					"title": "What Canonical Tags Can and Cannot Do",
					"excerpt": "A canonical tag is a strong hint about the preferred URL. It is not a directive, and it cannot fix a confused site on its own.",
					"featured_image": {
						"$media": {
							"url": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1499750310107-5fef28a66643?w=1200&h=800&fit=crop",
							"alt": "Laptop and coffee on a wooden table",
							"filename": "canonical.jpg"
						}
					},
					"content": [
						{
							"_type": "block",
							"_key": "k18",
							"style": "normal",
							"children": [
								{
									"_type": "span",
									"_key": "k19",
									"text": "A canonical tag tells search engines which URL you prefer when several show the same content."
								}
							]
						},
						{
							"_type": "block",
							"_key": "k20",
							"style": "h2",
							"children": [
								{
									"_type": "span",
									"_key": "k21",
									"text": "Why a canonical can be ignored"
								}
							]
						},
						{
							"_type": "block",
							"_key": "k22",
							"style": "normal",
							"children": [
								{
									"_type": "span",
									"_key": "k23",
									"text": "Search engines weigh it against other signals: internal links, redirects, sitemap entries and the content itself. When those disagree, your tag may lose."
								}
							]
						},
						{
							"_type": "block",
							"_key": "k24",
							"style": "h2",
							"children": [
								{
									"_type": "span",
									"_key": "k25",
									"text": "Keep the signals consistent"
								}
							]
						},
						{
							"_type": "block",
							"_key": "k30",
							"style": "normal",
							"children": [
								{
									"_type": "span",
									"_key": "k27",
									"text": "Link to the canonical URL, list only that URL in the sitemap, and redirect obvious duplicates. Our notes on "
								},
								{
									"_type": "span",
									"_key": "k28",
									"text": "XML sitemaps",
									"marks": [
										"k26"
									]
								},
								{
									"_type": "span",
									"_key": "k29",
									"text": " cover the sitemap side."
								}
							],
							"markDefs": [
								{
									"_type": "link",
									"_key": "k26",
									"href": "/posts/xml-sitemaps-are-hints"
								}
							]
						}
					]
				},
				"taxonomies": {
					"category": [
						"crawling"
					],
					"tag": [
						"canonicals"
					]
				},
				"bylines": [
					{
						"byline": "byline-editorial"
					}
				]
			},
			{
				"id": "post-robots",
				"slug": "how-to-read-robots-txt",
				"status": "published",
				"data": {
					"title": "How to Read a robots.txt File",
					"excerpt": "robots.txt controls crawling, not indexing. Mixing up those two jobs causes many avoidable problems.",
					"featured_image": {
						"$media": {
							"url": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1432821596592-e2c18b78144f?w=1200&h=800&fit=crop",
							"alt": "Notebook and pen on a desk",
							"filename": "robots.jpg"
						}
					},
					"content": [
						{
							"_type": "block",
							"_key": "k31",
							"style": "normal",
							"children": [
								{
									"_type": "span",
									"_key": "k32",
									"text": "The file is short, but small mistakes in it can have a large effect on how a site is crawled."
								}
							]
						},
						{
							"_type": "block",
							"_key": "k33",
							"style": "h2",
							"children": [
								{
									"_type": "span",
									"_key": "k34",
									"text": "Crawling is not indexing"
								}
							]
						},
						{
							"_type": "block",
							"_key": "k35",
							"style": "normal",
							"children": [
								{
									"_type": "span",
									"_key": "k36",
									"text": "A blocked URL can still appear in results if other pages link to it. To keep a page out of the index, allow crawling and use a noindex directive."
								}
							]
						},
						{
							"_type": "block",
							"_key": "k37",
							"style": "h2",
							"children": [
								{
									"_type": "span",
									"_key": "k38",
									"text": "Check it on every launch"
								}
							]
						},
						{
							"_type": "block",
							"_key": "k43",
							"style": "normal",
							"children": [
								{
									"_type": "span",
									"_key": "k40",
									"text": "Staging rules often reach production by accident. Add robots.txt to your launch checklist, along with the items in our "
								},
								{
									"_type": "span",
									"_key": "k41",
									"text": "CMS migration checklist",
									"marks": [
										"k39"
									]
								},
								{
									"_type": "span",
									"_key": "k42",
									"text": "."
								}
							],
							"markDefs": [
								{
									"_type": "link",
									"_key": "k39",
									"href": "/posts/cms-migration-seo-checklist"
								}
							]
						}
					]
				},
				"taxonomies": {
					"category": [
						"crawling"
					],
					"tag": [
						"audits"
					]
				},
				"bylines": [
					{
						"byline": "byline-editorial"
					}
				]
			},
			{
				"id": "post-redirects",
				"slug": "redirect-mapping-for-url-changes",
				"status": "published",
				"data": {
					"title": "Redirect Mapping for URL Changes",
					"excerpt": "Good redirects go straight to the closest matching page, in one hop, with the right status code.",
					"featured_image": {
						"$media": {
							"url": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1575026615908-666710ae5e47?w=1200&h=800&fit=crop",
							"alt": "Wrenches and hand tools hanging on a workshop wall",
							"filename": "redirects.jpg"
						}
					},
					"content": [
						{
							"_type": "block",
							"_key": "k44",
							"style": "normal",
							"children": [
								{
									"_type": "span",
									"_key": "k45",
									"text": "A redirect map is a plain table: old URL, new URL and status code. It is dull work, and it protects the value the old URLs built up."
								}
							]
						},
						{
							"_type": "block",
							"_key": "k46",
							"style": "h2",
							"children": [
								{
									"_type": "span",
									"_key": "k47",
									"text": "Choose the closest match"
								}
							]
						},
						{
							"_type": "block",
							"_key": "k48",
							"style": "normal",
							"children": [
								{
									"_type": "span",
									"_key": "k49",
									"text": "Send each old URL to the page that best replaces it. Sending everything to the homepage is often treated as a soft 404."
								}
							]
						},
						{
							"_type": "block",
							"_key": "k50",
							"style": "h2",
							"children": [
								{
									"_type": "span",
									"_key": "k51",
									"text": "Avoid chains"
								}
							]
						},
						{
							"_type": "block",
							"_key": "k52",
							"style": "normal",
							"children": [
								{
									"_type": "span",
									"_key": "k53",
									"text": "Every extra hop adds delay and another chance to fail. After a second migration, update the older rules so they point at the final URL."
								}
							]
						}
					]
				},
				"taxonomies": {
					"category": [
						"migrations"
					],
					"tag": [
						"redirects"
					]
				},
				"bylines": [
					{
						"byline": "byline-editorial"
					}
				]
			},
			{
				"id": "post-sitemaps",
				"slug": "xml-sitemaps-are-hints",
				"status": "published",
				"data": {
					"title": "XML Sitemaps Are Hints, Not Guarantees",
					"excerpt": "A sitemap helps discovery. It does not force indexing, so it should list only the URLs you want indexed.",
					"featured_image": {
						"$media": {
							"url": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1513542789411-b6a5d4f31634?w=1200&h=800&fit=crop",
							"alt": "Pencils and design tools on a desk",
							"filename": "sitemaps.jpg"
						}
					},
					"content": [
						{
							"_type": "block",
							"_key": "k54",
							"style": "normal",
							"children": [
								{
									"_type": "span",
									"_key": "k55",
									"text": "A sitemap tells search engines which URLs you consider important. Treat it as a clean list, not a dump of the database."
								}
							]
						},
						{
							"_type": "block",
							"_key": "k56",
							"style": "h2",
							"children": [
								{
									"_type": "span",
									"_key": "k57",
									"text": "What belongs in it"
								}
							]
						},
						{
							"_type": "block",
							"_key": "k58",
							"style": "normal",
							"children": [
								{
									"_type": "span",
									"_key": "k59",
									"text": "List indexable, canonical URLs that return 200. Leave out redirects, noindexed pages, drafts and duplicates."
								}
							]
						},
						{
							"_type": "block",
							"_key": "k60",
							"style": "h2",
							"children": [
								{
									"_type": "span",
									"_key": "k61",
									"text": "Use it as a diagnostic"
								}
							]
						},
						{
							"_type": "block",
							"_key": "k66",
							"style": "normal",
							"children": [
								{
									"_type": "span",
									"_key": "k63",
									"text": "Comparing sitemap URLs with indexed URLs shows where a site and search engines disagree. See how this connects to "
								},
								{
									"_type": "span",
									"_key": "k64",
									"text": "canonical tags",
									"marks": [
										"k62"
